            """Mauryan municipal administration (as in Megasthenes/Arthashastra traditions) featured appointed officials, committees for markets, sanitation, vital statistics, and strict regulation of trade — a bureaucratic city under imperial oversight. Today’s municipality is a constitutional local self-government unit (74th Amendment) with elected councils, ward representation, and functions in the 12th Schedule. Contrast: popular mandate vs imperial appointment; modern taxation/accountability vs ancient surveillance-regulation. Continuity: concern with drains, markets, and public order. Comparison highlights India’s long urban administrative imagination and the democratic leap of contemporary urban local bodies.""",
